# 0007. snacks.nvim for UI pieces, oil.nvim for files

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
UI pieces (start screen, notifications, prompts, pickers, buffer delete) came from separate
plugins or were missing; the telescope file browser made telescope load at startup.

## Decision
- snacks.nvim provides the start screen, notifications, rename box, code-action picker,
  buffer delete that keeps splits, word highlight/jumps, lazygit float and big-file handling.
  It loads at start with priority 1000.
- oil.nvim replaces telescope-file-browser: folders are edited as text.
- telescope stays for find/grep (`<C-p>`, `<C-f>`, `\f…`), loaded on first use.

## Alternatives
- telescope-file-browser: kept telescope in the startup path.

## Rationale
Fewer plugins for more features, one consistent look, faster start.

## Consequences
- snacks and oil are among the few `lazy = false` plugins ([0002](0002-lazy-nvim-pinned-and-lazy-loaded.adr)).

## References
- README "Design pass", `lua/plugins/ui.lua`, `lua/plugins/editor.lua`
